 is the quotient of $3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x-1$ divided by ${x}^{2}+x+1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069008 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d8bc05a-3c12-5aa5-909c-eac9c4d84a12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069008 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x-5 \\\\  & {x}^{2}+x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5{x}^{2}-4x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,5{x}^{2}-5x-5}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $3x-5,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $x+4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069009 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186065487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069009 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104250" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069009 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069009 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the remainder when $-2{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+1$ is divided by $2{x}^{2}-x+5?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069009 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b5c06d52-b891-50af-98a6-86efeb0cc9c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069009 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a coefficient of zero, as follows:\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+1=-2{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+0x+1\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+1 \\\\  & 2{x}^{2}-x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-2{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+0x+1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,2{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+0x+1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-x+5}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $-{x}^{2}+1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $x-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069010 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186065493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069010 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069010 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069010 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the remainder when  $-12{x}^{4}+28{x}^{3}-47{x}^{2}+25x-9$ is divided by $6{x}^{2}-5x+4?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069010 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f43b46ed-bff2-5d10-a08b-b040b0fe854b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069010 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2{x}^{2}+3x-4 \\\\  & 6{x}^{2}-5x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-12{x}^{4}+28{x}^{3}-47{x}^{2}+25x-\\phantom{0}9\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-12{x}^{4}+10{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,18{x}^{3}-39{x}^{2}+25x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{18{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+12x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-24{x}^{2}+13x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,24{x}^{2}+20x-16}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-7x+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $-2{x}^{2}+3x-4,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-7x+7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069669 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069669 #edb/ref 1061 18896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069669 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "44a9504c-2712-520b-9afa-31a3bf6cea61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069669 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069670 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069670 #edb/ref 1061 18897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069670 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9f200fd9-719c-597f-b531-42d1b3346597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069670 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069671 #edb/ref 1061 18898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069671 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b176dca5-6b75-5e46-ada1-b11bd84387bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069671 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069750 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069750 #edb/ref 1061 33336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069750 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6438e377-6aac-5674-a6de-e4d8421e658a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069750 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069974 #edb/ref 1064 "The long division method allows us to divide a polynomial by another nonlinear polynomial.\n\nFor example, suppose we want to find the quotient and remainder of the following division problem:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{-4x^3+4x^2+x+4}{4x^2-1}\n$$\n\nHere, the divisor is the quadratic polynomial $4x^2-1$. \n\nAgain, we follow a step-by-step process.\n\n**Step 1**\n\nWe start by writing the dividend and the divisor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**\n\nWe divide the leading term of the dividend $({\\color{red}{-4x^3}})$ by the leading term of the divisor $({\\color{blue}{4x^2}}).$ This gives $\\left(\\dfrac{\\color{red}{-4x^3}}{{\\color{blue}{4x^2}}}\\right)={\\color{#8b008b}{-x}}.$ We add this result to the quotient line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the $\\color{#8b008b}-x$ we just found by the full divisor ${\\color{blue}{4x^2}}-1.$ This gives ${\\color{#8b008b}-x}({\\color{blue}{4x^2}}-1)=-4x^3+x.$ We place this underneath the dividend, being sure to match the terms. Notice that we include a zero coefficient for the $x^2$ term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+x}_{―}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we subtract $-4x^3+0x^2+x$ from $-4x^3+4x^2+x+4$ and get $4x^2+0x+4\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**\n\nWe now repeat the process. The new dividend is ${\\color{red}{4x^2}}+0x+4.$\n\nWe divide the leading term of the dividend $({\\color{red}{4x^2}})$ by the leading term of the divisor $({\\color{blue}{4x^2}}).$ This gives $\\left(\\dfrac{{\\color{red}{4x^2}}}{{\\color{blue}{4x^2}}}\\right)={\\color{#8b008b}{1}}.$ We  add this result to the quotient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x+1 \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the ${\\color{#8b008b}{1}}$ we just found by the full divisor ${\\color{blue}{4x^2}}-1.$ This gives ${\\color{#8b008b}{1}}({\\color{blue}{4x^2}}-1)=4x^2-1.$ We place this result underneath the dividend:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x+1 \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+0x-1}_{―}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we subtract $4x^2+0x-1$ from $4x^2+0x+4$ to get ${\\color{red}{5}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x+1 \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+0x-1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're left with the constant $\\color{red}5$, which has a smaller degree than the divisor. So, the division is complete.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n- the quotient of the polynomial division is ${\\color{blue}{-x+1}},$ and\n\n- the remainder is ${\\color{red}{5}}.$\n\nOur complete result can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{-4x^3+4x^2+x+4}{4x^2-1}={\\color{blue}{-x+1}} + \\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{4x^2-1}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069974 #edb/ref 1065 3382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069974 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "65b9f3fa-d1aa-5799-bc53-d2a843778980" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069974 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552876 #edb/ref 1080 "-x+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552876 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552876 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "082d317c-2419-5ca8-be39-772653d8c4bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552879 #edb/ref 1080 "2{x}^{2}+2+\\frac{x-3}{2{x}^{2}-x-2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552879 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552879 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0aa146ec-87f8-5eb8-949b-2bcb1af0b5c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552880 #edb/ref 1080 "x+2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552880 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552880 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ba2998d-4829-5f91-add0-da81bbe37687" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552914 #edb/ref 1080 "4x-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552914 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552914 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1ac723e7-52c4-54cb-a3f4-40cdbf0e98e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552921 #edb/ref 1080 "-x+3-\\frac{7{x}^{2}+x-2}{-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552921 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552921 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1cfa05af-ca7a-571e-9c6e-43a341402226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552953 #edb/ref 1080 "x+7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552953 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552953 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2d59bce2-4bc6-566a-bf9e-3a8d96684f51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552957 #edb/ref 1080 "x+2" #ed